<h2>How Many Do You See? PLC Activity</h2>
<p><strong>Original 2021 learning goal:</strong> Apply understanding of equal groups and multiplication to create a How Many Do You See activity.</p>
<p>Warm-up How Many Do You See: Equal Groups (10 minutes). Discuss how a group of dots may be perceived through different equal-group arrangements. The original displayed source dot image&#x27;s pixel geometry has not been verified.</p>
<h3>How Many Do You See: Equal Groups</h3><p>Discuss the original teacher-provided dot image and explain valid totals and grouping strategies. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<h3>Design Your How Many Do You See</h3><p>Draw a dot array with equal groups and list at least two ways to see it. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<h3>Facilitate Your How Many Do You See</h3><p>Flash your drawing, give 30 seconds quiet thinking, redisplay, allow peer talk and record alternate groupings. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
